# CoreDNS configuration. SKELETON.
#
# Two blocks, and the split is the lesson: authoritative for one zone, a
# forwarder for everything else.

# TODO 5 -- the authoritative block.
#
#   lab.test:53 {
#       file /etc/coredns/zones/lab.test.zone
#       log
#       errors
#   }
#
# `file` makes CoreDNS authoritative: it answers from the zone and returns
# NXDOMAIN for names it does not hold, rather than asking anyone else. That
# refusal is the point - it is what 3.5's "reject names it does not know"
# depends on.

# TODO 6 -- the forwarder.
#
#   . {
#       forward . 10.1.0.1
#       cache 30
#       log
#       errors
#   }
#
# Everything not in lab.test goes upstream. Get this wrong and the host resolves
# web.lab.test but not github.com.
#
# NEVER forward to 127.0.0.53. That is systemd-resolved, which 2.3 is about to
# point back at CoreDNS - the loop resolves nothing and is invisible in the logs.
# 10.1.0.1 is the gateway (network-plan row 1); 8.8.8.8 is what the old build
# used and is still in 05-cloudstack-bootstrap.conf.
#
# `cache 30` is deliberate while iterating: a long TTL means every mistake you
# make is still being answered five minutes after you fixed it.
